This software is NOT open source. It is licensed, not sold.

1. DEFINITIONS
   "Software" means the MV Data Governance program: its source and compiled
   code, the engine (catalog, quality, lineage, glossary, policies, profiling,
   MDM, connectors, exporters), the interface, the API, the documentation and
   associated materials. "Licensor" is the copyright holder named above.
   "You" is the individual or entity using the Software.

2. LICENSE GRANTED
   a) Demo / evaluation version: you are granted a limited, non-exclusive,
      non-transferable, revocable license to install and use the Software for
      internal evaluation purposes.
   b) Production, commercial or organization-wide use requires a valid paid
      license from the Licensor. Without such a license, productive use is not
      authorized.

3. RESTRICTIONS
   Except with the Licensor's prior written permission, you may NOT:
   a) Redistribute, publish, sublicense, sell, rent, lend or otherwise make the
      Software available to third parties, by any means.
   b) Reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, deobfuscate or otherwise
      attempt to derive the source code of parts distributed in compiled form,
      except to the extent applicable law expressly permits and such right
      cannot be excluded by contract.
   c) Create derivative works, adaptations or competing products based on the
      Software or on its architecture, rules or business logic.
   d) Remove, alter or obscure copyright notices, trademarks, attributions or
      this license text.
   e) Use the Software to provide an equivalent service to third parties
      (SaaS, hosting, packaged consulting) without a commercial license.

4. OWNERSHIP
   The Licensor retains title and all intellectual property rights in the
   Software. This license transfers no ownership to you, only the usage rights
   expressly described.

5. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
   This license does NOT apply to third-party components included in or used by
   the Software, which are governed by their own licenses:

   a) Open source dependencies (Streamlit, pandas, NumPy, Plotly, FastAPI,
      uvicorn, openpyxl, XlsxWriter, PyArrow, SQLAlchemy, keyring, the MCP SDK,
      among others): each retains its original license.
   b) Sample datasets shipped with the Software:
      - "Dirty Cafe Sales" (Kaggle, by Ahmed Mohamed) — CC BY-SA 4.0,
        attribution required.
      - "Bank Marketing" (UCI Machine Learning Repository; S. Moro, P. Rita,
        P. Cortez) — CC BY 4.0, attribution required.
      - openFDA NDC Directory (api.fda.gov) — U.S. Government work, public
        domain. openFDA warns these data are NOT validated for medical
        decisions.
      - Food safety control data (Uruguay) — open government data.
      Each dataset's attribution and license are shown inside the program
      itself. The Licensor claims no ownership over them.

   Demo data generated by the Software is 100% synthetic and contains no real
   personal information.

6. NO WARRANTY
   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. The Software is a
   data governance support tool: it does not replace professional judgment,
   human review or the regulatory compliance owed by your organization.

7. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY
   To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the Licensor shall not be
   liable for indirect, incidental, special, punitive or consequential damages,
   nor for lost profits or lost data, arising from the use of or inability to
   use the Software.

8. TERMINATION
   This license terminates automatically if you breach any of its terms. Upon
   termination you must cease all use and uninstall the Software.

9. GOVERNING LAW
   This license is governed by the laws of the jurisdiction of the Licensor's
   domicile, without prejudice to any mandatory consumer rights granted to you
   by applicable law.

Commercial licensing contact: the holder named in the copyright notice.

